# Agent skills (bale-med)

This repo ships project skills under `.cursor/skills/`. Setup for issue tracker, triage labels, and domain docs is in `docs/agents/` and `AGENTS.md`.

## Auto routing (default)

Follow `.cursor/rules/auto-skill-routing.mdc`. When context matches, read the matching `.cursor/skills/*/SKILL.md` and run it — no `/skill-name` required.

## When the user asks about skills, setup, or workflow

1. Read `docs/agents/GETTING-STARTED.md` if you need the full guide (Persian + English).
2. Tell the user that **most workflow skills do not auto-run** — they must type `/skill-name` in Agent chat (e.g. `/ask-matt`, `/grilling`, `/triage`).
3. Skills that **can** auto-apply when relevant: `tdd`, `diagnosing-bugs`, `domain-modeling`, `grilling`, `codebase-design`, and similar skills **without** `disable-model-invocation: true`.
4. If skills are missing, the user likely needs branch `cursor/install-mattpocock-skills-74e7` or `main` after [PR #29](https://github.com/hosseintajdari/bale-med/pull/29) is merged, then **Developer: Reload Window** in Cursor.
5. Verify discovery: Cursor sidebar → **Customize → Skills** — project skills from `.cursor/skills/` should appear.

## Pharmacy safety (always)

Do not use skills to bypass safety boundaries in `docs/SAFETY_RULES.md` — no diagnosis, dosage advice, or prescription replacement.
